codex
A feasibility check exposed an important issue before the main run: unconstrained independent random assignments are geometrically legal but collapse `served_PHY` (for example, 1–10 served users on `w1/s0`) and therefore are not admissible under the unchanged baseline guard. I’m correcting the start generator to a deterministic, non-objective random walk from the nearest baseline: one seeded shuffled pass over users, one uniform legal-option draw per user, accepting a perturbation only if the exact evaluator says it remains physically valid and satisfies the original guard. This preserves the rule and produces genuinely feasible starts; the random path can differ by provisioning rule because feasibility itself differs.
apply patch
